# Transcripts — raw source, not knowledge base. Read them to build/update the note,
# fold the important content (instructor quotes, emphasis, off-slide clarifications)
# into the session note, then don't commit. The note is the record, not the transcript.
# Transcripts are raw source: read them, fold them into the note, discard.
# The .gitkeep exception is load-bearing — the directory's CONTENTS are ignored,
# so without it the folder wouldn't exist on a fresh clone and there'd be nowhere
# obvious to drop a transcript. This is the only .gitkeep in the repo that has a
# job; git tracks files, not folders, so every other directory appears by itself
# the moment it holds something real.
2026-2027-Sem1/*/source/transcripts/*
!2026-2027-Sem1/*/source/transcripts/.gitkeep

# Tool dependencies — reinstall with `cd tools && npm install`
tools/node_modules/
tools/package-lock.json
